cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CrYAL: Crystal Structure Prediction via Active Learning"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself
  and the accompanying article.
type: software
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of BACH (Bayesian Active Crystal Hopping), a blind
  crystal-structure-prediction workflow for molecular organic crystals. It
  couples symmetry-aware random generation, relaxation on a machine-learned
  interatomic potential (MACE-OFF23 through LAMMPS), and a Gaussian-process
  surrogate with an Expected-Improvement acquisition function that learns
  online which regions of the crystallographic search space are favorable.
authors:
